  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_028 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200 + ViT_L, transformer, concat) is the current best at 0.721 acc / 0.681 F1. All high-performing experiments to date use concat fusion; weighted fusion has never been tested in the multiprofile + transformer regime. Question: Does changing fusion from concat to weighted (while holding every other variable identical to config_028) improve performance, or is concat already sufficient? This isolates the fusion axis cleanly. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a single-variable change from the current best, directly testing a design axis (fusion) that is completely unexplored in the high-performing regime. If weighted fusion helps, we gain a clear improvement; if not, we eliminate fusion as a lever and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder alternatives (scgpt, pca_n2000). Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step."
}

